# --- MITRE ATT&CK vendored artifacts (gate G0.1): preserve byte-for-byte. ---
# The bundle's SHA-256 is the reproducibility anchor recorded in manifest.json
# (docs/architecture/11-attack-knowledge-versioning.md). Marking these
# "binary" disables Git's line-ending conversion (autocrlf) entirely, on any
# platform or local git config, so a checkout can never silently change the
# artifact's bytes and invalidate the recorded hash.
data/attack/**/*.json binary

# --- Sigma detection content (ADR-0007 D7): the vendored release archive is
# SHA-256-pinned and the generated pack/report must regenerate byte-for-byte
# (tests/test_sigma_import.py), so no line-ending conversion either. ---
data/detection/**/*.zip binary
data/detection/**/*.json binary

# --- Real telemetry samples (ADR-0008 D2.3): SHA-256-pinned, byte-for-byte. ---
data/telemetry-samples/**/*.zip binary
data/telemetry-samples/**/*.json binary
